{"campground":{"facility_id":"233716","parent_asset_id":"511","inventory_type_id":"3","facility_type":"STANDARD","order_components":{"camping_equipment":true,"group_leader_address":true,"group_leader_details":true,"group_size":true,"num_vehicles":true,"pass":true},"facility_lookups":null,"facility_description_map":{"Facilities":"\u003cp\u003eThe campground offers 51 electric sites, one group site, and one day-use group picnic shelter with water and electric hookups. 23 non-electric sites are available, many of which have water hookups. Amenities include flush toilets, showers, drinking water, a boat ramp and playground.\u003c/p\u003e\n","Natural Features":"\u003cp\u003eThe park is situated on the lakeshore among rolling hills covered with cedar, live, and post oak trees.  Many deer like to enjoy their stay at Lofers West along with the racoons and foxes.\u003c/p\u003e\n","Nearby Attractions":"\n","Overview":"Lofers Bend West Campground is located on Whitney Lake on the Brazos River in Central Texas. Over two million people visit Whitney Lake each year to enjoy the plethora of recreational activities and scenic beauty the lake provides.","Recreation":"Boating, fishing, swimming, canoeing and kayaking are popular activities at Whitney Lake. Anglers can fish for a variety of bass, crappie and catfish."},"facility_name":"LOFERS BEND WEST","city":"","state":"","facility_adaaccess":"N","facility_directions":"From I-35 in Hillsboro, take Hwy 22 west 12 miles to Whitney, continue 7 miles past Whitney, and turn right before dam. Follow park road to 4-way stop. Turn left for West Lofers or right for East Lofers.","facility_email":"","facility_email_display":false,"facility_map_url":"","facility_latitude":31.8852778,"facility_longitude":-97.3611111,"facility_phone":"254-622-3332","facility_reservation_url":"","facility_use_fee_description":"","cancellation_description":"","alternate_names":"LOFW,WHITNEY LAKE,LAKE WHITNEY,WEST LOFERS BEND,LOFERS BEND EAST,EAST LOFERS BEND,LOFER